MESSAGE(HELP_INDEX, "Topic help\r\nHELP ACCOUNT   Registration, login and passwords\r\nHELP READ      Reading, navigation and search\r\nHELP UNREAD    Read state and unread navigation\r\nHELP CONTENT   Article changes, cross-board search, sequential reading\r\nHELP CHAT      Shared chat room\r\nHELP POST      Posting, replies and editing\r\nHELP EDITOR    Shared editor and auxiliary commands\r\nHELP DRAFT     Saving and resuming drafts\r\nHELP FILES     File vault and downloads\r\nHELP GATHER    Gather message board\r\nHELP SETTINGS  Language, paging and preferences\r\nHELP MAIL      Member mail\r\nHELP PROFILE   Public profiles\r\nHELP TALK      Private talk\r\nHELP ADMIN     Administrator commands\r\nHELP shows this index; ? shows the current menu; MENU opens the main screen.\r\nShortcuts apply at the menu prompt, not inside input fields or the body.\r\n")
MESSAGE(HELP_READ, "RTBBS-style boards and reading\r\nMain B / BOARDS lists boards. Select a number or BOARD id.\r\nBoard L / NOTES lists base notes. Select an article number or READ id.\r\nI / INFO: information. E: new post. R: reply to the selected article.\r\nN asks for a date. Empty input starts CHECK ARTICLES HERE for the current board.\r\nF asks for an author login. T starts newest-first sequential reading.\r\nWhile reading: Enter next, P previous, L repeat, F nonstop.\r\nD / PARENT: parent. A / CHILD: first reply. TREE: reply tree.\r\n+/- or +N/-N while reading changes direction/offset in article-ID order.\r\nG / GET [id]: copy into the shared edit buffer. Read permission suffices; BUFFER edits it, /BUFFER imports it into a later draft. K: withdraw as author, admin or inherited SIGOP (Y confirms).\r\nE while reading: moderator title/author editing.\r\n0 returns from reading to notes, then to main. MENU goes to main. ? shows screen help.\r\nSEARCH text searches this board. FIND HERE|ALL|SUBTREE author|* text|*.\r\nSCAN [ASC|DESC] HERE|ALL|SUBTREE author|* text|* selects sequential reading.\r\nDuring SCAN: Enter/CONTINUE next, F nonstop, STOP/0/Q stops the sequence.\r\nO/Q at an ordinary menu ask Y/N before disconnecting. Reading does not mark articles read.\r\nSEEN marks read; NEW reads unread; UNREAD lists unread; NEXTBOARD changes unread board.\r\nList + fetches more results; Enter at the screen pager continues that screen.\r\nNEWS [ALL|HERE] YYYY-MM-DD filters from configured local midnight.\r\n")
MESSAGE(HELP_UNREAD, "Read state and new-item checks\r\nUNREAD lists unread articles. NEW reads next unread. SEEN marks selected article read.\r\nUNSEEN id marks unread. NEW thread-id reads unread within a thread.\r\nNOTES UNREAD lists unread threads. NEXTBOARD visits another unread board.\r\nReading alone does not mark read. Former Liner notes U/F/S/A/K/J shortcuts are retired.\r\nCHECK ARTICLES / MAIL / FILES starts from the saved checkpoint for that type.\r\nCHECK NEXT continues. In MANUAL mode, CHECK DONE saves the start timestamp after the last page.\r\nCHECK CANCEL or disconnect leaves the checkpoint unchanged.\r\n\r\nstage67: Menu sessions automatically save the start timestamp after displaying the final result. Q at a result pager, CHECK CANCEL or disconnect before completion does not advance it. CHECK ARTICLES HERE|SUBTREE|ALL and CHECK FILES path keep independent checkpoints. CHECKMODE MANUAL requires CHECK DONE; AUTO commits automatically. Raw sessions default to MANUAL.\r\n")
MESSAGE(HELP_POST, "Posting, replies and editing\r\nE at the board menu prompts for a title; R replies to the selected article. POST title / REPLY id title also work.\r\nIn the body editor (title: 80 bytes; body: 262144 bytes including line endings):\r\nA line containing only . posts; /PREVIEW previews; /CANCEL discards the in-memory draft.\r\n/TITLE title changes the title; /LINES lists numbered lines.\r\n/REPLACE number text replaces a line; /DELETE number removes it.\r\n/INSERT number text inserts a line, including after the last line.\r\n/UNDO reverts one edit; /SAVE stores a member draft.\r\n/HELP shows this help without changing the body or Undo.\r\nDouble a leading dot to enter it literally. //HELP and //SAVE enter /HELP and /SAVE as text.\r\nOrdinary HELP and menu shortcuts are body text while editing.\r\nHelp is not executed during password input.\r\nEDITOR BETA / LINE; /EDITOR BETA / LINE while composing. Beta: // finish, /E line mode, /N clear, /M numbering. Line: nn select, E[n] edit, A append / U timed receive, I[n] insert, N clear, D range delete, L range list, Q range quote, S search, M numbering, 0 confirm. Ranges: L3-5, D-2. // returns from input. /SAVE /CANCEL /UNDO /PREVIEW /TITLE remain available.\r\nBUFFER edits a shared 262144-byte buffer. In editors, /BUFFER imports it and /TOBUFFER copies the current text into it. /SAVE or . commits BIOEDIT and FILEINFOEDIT documents. /ONLINE /W /STATUS /TALK [connection] /MEMO text /CALL are available while editing. Ending talk returns to the document.\r\n\r\nGuest posting requires explicit BOARDGUEST permission. HANDLE name lasts for the connection; author is recorded as guest:name.\r\n\r\nBeta // opens confirmation: W commit / E edit / 0 cancel. The extended . command commits immediately.\r\n")
MESSAGE(HELP_DRAFT, "Saving and resuming drafts\r\n/SAVE in the editor stores one draft per member. Saving is manual.\r\nAt the normal prompt, DRAFT shows its revision and deletion instructions; RESUME resumes it.\r\nDRAFT DELETE revision removes it only if that revision is current.\r\nPosting leaves the stored copy intact. Confirm the post, then delete the copy explicitly.\r\n/CANCEL or disconnect keeps the stored copy; unsaved additions are lost.\r\nA new draft cannot overwrite an existing copy: RESUME it or delete it first.\r\nOn conflict, keep needed text using /PREVIEW, then /CANCEL before DRAFT and RESUME.\r\nSave/resume rechecks permissions. Undo history is not stored.\r\n")
MESSAGE(HELP_SETTINGS, "Language, paging and preferences\r\nLANG ja / LANG en selects Japanese or English.\r\nPAGER ON / PAGER OFF controls screen paging (initially OFF).\r\nWhile paging: Enter continues, Q closes the display, OFF flushes the rest.\r\nClosing help preserves article selection and result-page position.\r\nPAGER SIZE columns rows sets dimensions; Telnet also supports NAWS.\r\nPREFS inspects stored settings; PREFS SAVE stores language and paging ON/OFF for your account.\r\nPREFS LOAD reloads them. Login restores them too.\r\nRAW selects protocol output; MENU returns to menus. QUIT / O / Q disconnects at the normal prompt.\r\nPREFS SAVE also stores editor type, columns and rows.\r\n\r\nMENUMODE BEGINNER / STANDARD / EXPERT: home menu always / initially / explicitly; saved per account.\r\nLOGOUT / QUIT saves display preferences before leaving; abrupt disconnects are not guaranteed.\r\nGAMES lists native games; DOOR id starts one. Exit or Ctrl-] returns to the BBS.\r\n\r\nD in Settings displays actual language, editor, menu verbosity, paging, screen dimensions, timezone and transfer protocol. S reads external sysinfo.txt; V shows version. O/Q ask Y/N; QUIT is immediate. goodbye.txt is displayed on exit.\r\n")
MESSAGE(HELP_ACCOUNT, "Registration, login and passwords\r\nA / REGISTER name creates an account; LOGIN name logs in.\r\nNames: 1-32 lowercase ASCII letters, digits, _ or -. Passwords: 8-128 bytes.\r\nEnter passwords only after the password prompt, not on the command line.\r\n# / ACCOUNT shows your account; LOGOUT logs out.\r\nPASSWD prompts for the current password, new password and confirmation.\r\nA successful change revokes your other sessions; this session remains logged in.\r\n/CANCEL cancels menu input.\r\nLogin unread and saved-draft notices reflect the authentication-time state.\r\nRIGHTS shows your level and groups. Registration may require approval or be closed.\r\nUSERLOG [ID] [cursor] shows your connection history; USERSTATS shows login count and usage. + continues history.\r\nUSERTABLE [member|ALL] [cursor]: login, logout, seconds, login count and transport on one row per login. Other members require --userlog-public. Unknown baud rates are not invented.\r\n\r\nRETIRE CONFIRM ends your membership and disables login. Existing articles, correspondent mail and IDs remain; login names cannot be reused. Protected administrators cannot retire through this command.\r\n\r\nWith automatic IDs, REGISTER or A issues a u000001-style login name. The optional detailed form collects profile fields, referring BBS and a private SYSOP note. Enter skips a field; /CANCEL aborts. Personal name/address/phone/birthday fields are private by default.\r\n\r\nAutomatic IDs: --id-mode auto --id-prefix bbs --id-digits 5 issues bbs00001-style names. --id-first sysop names only the first account in an empty member store; administrator rights still require admins configuration. Existing and retired IDs are unchanged.\r\nDetailed applications show all entered details before Y confirms, E restarts editing or /CANCEL aborts; password entry follows confirmation.\r\n--rtbbs-member-policy makes USERLOG/USERTABLE available to registered members. Default access stays self/admin. This option never changes saved profile visibility.\r\n")
MESSAGE(HELP_ADMIN, "Administration\r\n$ opens the administration menu. Choose 1..5 by task; 0 returns.\r\n1 Members / 2 Boards / 3 Vault / 4 Connections / 5 History and maintenance\r\nHELP ADMINMEMBERS / ADMINBOARDS / ADMINFILES / ADMINCONNECTIONS / ADMINSTORAGE\r\nOperations still require the stated target and confirmation. See HELP SIGOP for delegated scope.\r\n")
MESSAGE(HELP_UNKNOWN, "Unknown help topic. Use HELP for the topic index.\r\n")
MESSAGE(HELP_CLOSED, "Help closed.\r\n")
