MESSAGE(HELP_FILES, "FILEBOARDS: accessible file boards. ZUPLOADIN path|description (UIN in vault): upload into a board. Parent read permissions apply; FILESIN includes children.\r\nFile vault\r\nF or VAULT opens the vault menu. L lists, a number opens file actions, FILE id shows details, + continues, S text searches, C lists categories, I displays the current board information.\r\nU asks for protocol and description for the current board; D number downloads. 0 returns to the parent; at the root it returns to BBS.\r\nZUPLOAD [description] / ZDOWNLOAD number [filename] also work directly. One file, up to 1 GiB.\r\nRequires an enabled server connector and a ZMODEM-capable terminal with Telnet BINARY.\r\nWait for the published/sent receipt before treating a transfer as successful.\r\nFILES / FILE number / FILESEARCH text / FILECATEGORIES / FILESIN category remain available.\r\nLine-v1 and binary-v1 remain available to dedicated clients.\r\nN YYYY-MM-DD / FILENEWS YYYY-MM-DD: new files since configured local midnight. \r\nBATCH ADD id, BATCH REMOVE id, BATCH LIST, BATCH CLEAR, BATCH SEND: up to 16 selected files / 16 GiB total. Duplicate filenames receive an ID prefix. A failed batch may already have delivered some files.\r\nZUPLOADBATCH board|description: upload up to 16 files / 16 GiB. ZRESUME board|original description resumes an interrupted single-file upload or publication; select the same original file. Use - for the root board.\r\nZUPLOADBATCHRESUME board|original description: resume batch transfer/publication; select the original file set.\r\nFILESTATS [ID|ALL] [cursor] shows confirmed download counts. + continues. Failed, skipped and legacy unacknowledged transfers are not counted.\r\nFILEDESC id description / FILEDELETE id CONFIRM: owner with read/upload rights, or administrator. Deletion is permanent.\r\nFILESEARCH *.LZH / FILESEARCH file?.txt: case-insensitive filename wildcards. FILEASCII id ON|OFF; FILETYPE id [byte-offset] displays text. FILEBOARDINFO path shows the guide. PROTOCOL ZMODEM|XMODEM|YMODEM|YMODEM-G|MLINK|TEXT selects transfer mode. DOWNLOAD id; UPLOAD path|description; UPLOADBATCH path|description. XMODEM/TEXT uploads use path|filename|bytes|description (TEXT size 0 reads until Ctrl-Z). BATCH SEND uses the selected protocol, except XMODEM/TEXT. Existing ZUPLOAD commands always use ZMODEM.\r\nBATCH MATCH *.LZH replaces selection with matches (up to 16 files/16 GiB). + continues FILETYPE.\r\nVault moderators may use FILEOWNER id member, FILEBOARDNAME path|title, and FILEINFOEDIT path. Vault and article-board moderator assignments are separate.\r\n\r\nFILEUNLOCK path: enter the shared password privately, unlocking any protected ancestors first. Grants are connection-local and invalidated on password change or logout.\r\nFILERENAME id filename: administrator or inherited SIGOP changes the public name without changing the blob or ID.\r\nFILEBOARDPASS path / FILEBOARDPASS path NONE CONFIRM sets/clears its password. FILEBOARDOPTIONS path|BOARD or MENU order retained-downloads sets node type, order and receipt retention; 0 keeps all receipts. Lifetime download counts are preserved. MENU nodes reject uploads.\r\nCHECK FILES uses the previous file checkpoint. Default total storage quota is 16 GiB; existing limits.conf overrides it.\r\n\r\nRTBBS keys: main F; vault L list, U upload, D download, B batch screen, N date, I current-board info, 0 back. FILEBOARDS lists boards. A bare number opens file actions; FILE id only shows details. U/D use PROTOCOL; ZUPLOAD/ZDOWNLOAD always use ZMODEM.\r\n\r\nFILEBOARD path (- for root) selects the current file board for L/I/U/S/N. Search/news include descendants and enforce read permissions. FILESEARCH path|query and FILENEWS path|YYYY-MM-DD combine scope and filtering. Dates use the server timezone.\r\nU/UB asks protocol, description and (XMODEM/TEXT only) filename and exact size. B opens add/remove/match/list/clear/send choices. /CANCEL aborts.\r\nlimits.conf applies equally to vault/mail and transfer protocols. XMODEM/TEXT transfer one file at a time.\r\n\r\nBATCH LIST shows DONE (confirmed) and PENDING. SEND retries only pending files; completed receipts are not counted twice. To download a completed file again, REMOVE then ADD it, or CLEAR and select again. Selection state lasts for the current connection.\r\n\r\nAfter selecting a file: T display; S checksum/C CRC/X 1K/Y YMODEM/G YMODEM-g/Z ZMODEM/M M-LINK; B add to batch; E description; K delete; 0 back.\r\nDIR lists immediate child boards; select a displayed number to enter. CD child-path enters a child; 0 or CD .. returns to its parent. At root, 0 exits the vault.\r\nBatch screen: D choose protocol and send; L list; C confirmed clear; M copy into a managed board. Add/remove/MATCH are also available.\r\nBATCH MATCH searches only the current board, unlike recursive FILESEARCH. DOS masks compare name/extension separately; *.* includes extensionless files; ? can match trailing padding.\r\nFILECOPY id destination / BATCH COPY destination require management rights at both ends. Publisher, description, timestamp and ASCII attribute survive; the new ID starts its own download count at zero.\r\nPROTOCOL XMODEM-SUM / XMODEM / XMODEM-1K. Uploads require exact size and filename. The receiving peer negotiates checksum versus CRC; 1K requests 1024-byte blocks.\r\nLists include attributes, confirmed download count and description. FILE shows registration PROTOCOL; FILEAUDIT Q records its changes. Older imports are UNKNOWN; administrative copies are COPY.\r\nEach confirmed file receives a durable receipt even if a later file fails. DONE is excluded from retry; incomplete files remain PENDING. Copy completion is separate from download completion. Selection is connection-local.\r\n\r\nBare ZRESUME uses the current file board and saved description. ZRESUME board also reuses the description. Direct ZUPLOAD targets the root: use ZRESUME -. Reception times out after 120 seconds without file progress. Ask the administrator about resume receiver verification errors.\r\n")
