MESSAGE(CHAT_FULL, "Chat room unavailable.\r\n")
MESSAGE(HELP_CHAT, "Chat room (active members only)\r\nCHAT enters the shared room. Type a line to send it.\r\nW or /WHO: all logged-in connections; ? or /HELP: this help.\r\n// or /LEAVE: return to BBS; /QUIT: disconnect.\r\n/LANG ja or /LANG en: change display language.\r\n/SAY text: send W, ?, //, or slash-prefixed text literally.\r\nUp to 512 UTF-8 bytes per line; at least 0.5 seconds between messages.\r\nThe last 20 room events are shown on entry. Public chat can be logged using --chat-log; private talk is not logged.\r\nThe in-memory replay is cleared when the last participant leaves or the server stops; disk logs remain.\r\nHandles are taken at entry; login names identify members.\r\nT or /TALK: select a connection number; T number or /TALK number selects directly.\r\n/REPLY selects the most recent private sender. Private text is never in room history.\r\nInside private talk, // or /END returns to the room; /LEAVE leaves the room.\r\nUnavailable targets block text until you return or select again. /SAY stays private.\r\nPrivate recipients can be logged-in members outside this room. CALL notifies available administrators.\r\n /TALK OFF|ON: disable/enable private reception; /MUTE login: hide their private and public speech; /UNMUTE login: restore; /MUTES: list. Settings are saved automatically and shared across your connections. Presence remains visible.\r\nFrom BBS: TALK [connection] for outside-room talk; ONLINE lists logged-in connections; /REPLY replies. // returns. Busy editing/password/transfer sessions do not receive private messages.\r\nFrom the BBS screen: MEMO [text] sets/clears a connection memo; ONLINE shows it. CALL [reason] notifies available administrators, once per 30 seconds. Disabled with chat.\r\nLegacy keys: D calls SYSOP, # shows connection status, \\ enters a connection memo (`` also accepted).\r\n\r\nW lists all connections, including members outside chat. # displays current time, connection duration, online count and own usage totals. T [number] sends one private line then returns to chat. /TALK [number] remains a continuing private conversation; from BBS use TALK [number]. \\ enters a connection memo.\r\n")
