MESSAGE(MAIL_SENT, "Mail %u saved and sent.\r\n")
MESSAGE(MAIL_DELETED, "Mail %u deleted.\r\n")
MESSAGE(MAIL_NOTICE, "Unread mail: %u. Use MAIL to open your mailbox.\r\n")
MESSAGE(HELP_MAIL, "Member mail\r\nMAIL opens the mailbox. L lists, N asks for a date, T reads newest first, number reads, + continues.\r\nE prompts for recipient and subject, then body. R number replies to received mail.\r\nK number confirms deletion for both parties; either sender or recipient can delete.\r\n0 exits. Also: MAIL SEND login subject / MAIL READ number / MAIL REPLY number / MAIL DELETE number.\r\nMAIL SENT / MAIL INBOX / MAIL UNREAD filter lists. Only the recipient marks a message read by opening it.\r\nA single . sends; /CANCEL aborts. /PREVIEW and line editing work; /SAVE saves a private draft and exits. MAIL DRAFT shows its revision; MAIL RESUME continues; MAIL DRAFT DELETE revision removes it.\r\nMAIL NOTIFY shows the setting; MAIL NOTIFY ON / OFF changes arrival notifications.\r\nMAIL SEARCH text searches your sent/received subjects and bodies. + continues. Case-sensitive.\r\nMail attachments: ZMAILUPLOAD [description] stages a private file. MAIL FILES lists your files. In the mail editor use /ATTACH id or /DETACH, then /SAVE or send. ZMAILDOWNLOAD id downloads an attachment. MAIL DROP id CONFIRM reclaims your unreferenced file. Up to 16 files per message, each up to 1 GiB; sender and recipient only, including no SYSOP override.\r\nZMAILRESUME original description: resume an interrupted attachment upload; select the same original file.\r\nMAIL NEWS YYYY-MM-DD lists received mail since configured timezone midnight, including read mail; + continues. SYSOPMAIL title composes mail even as guest to the active administrator with the lowest member ID.\r\n\r\nRepeat /ATTACH ID for up to 16 attachments. Duplicate IDs are ignored. /DETACH ID removes one; /DETACH removes all. Attachments survive saved drafts and resume. Only sender/recipient can read them; storage is reclaimed after the final mail/draft reference is removed.\r\n\r\nMAIL SCAN ASC / MAIL SCAN DESC  reads continuously. Enter/CONTINUE, +/-, +N/-N and STOP work as for articles.\r\nMAIL GET [message-id] / G imports an authorized body into your common edit buffer; use /BUFFER in the next editor.\r\nZMAILDOWNLOADALL message-id downloads up to 16 attachments in one ZMODEM session, up to 16 GiB total. Duplicate names receive an ID prefix. Only sender/recipient may download; SYSOP has no exception.\r\nCHECK MAIL from the main menu uses the saved mail checkpoint.\r\n\r\nF during MAIL SCAN reads continuously; input stops it.\r\nZMAILUPLOADBATCH description receives up to 16 private attachment files. Use MAILFILES for IDs and /ATTACH id to attach.\r\nZMAILRESUMEBATCH description resumes the same batch with the same description and file set.\r\n\r\nN asks for a date (empty: CHECK MAIL). MAIL NEXT reads unread; MAIL LATEST reads one latest message.\r\n\r\nWhile reading: Enter next, P previous, L repeat, F nonstop from next, +/- or +N/-N changes direction/offset. MAIL LIST returns to the list. G imports into the common buffer; use /BUFFER in a later editor.\r\nMAILUPLOAD / MAILUPLOADBATCH / MAILDOWNLOAD / MAILDOWNLOADALL use PROTOCOL. Upload arguments: description (XMODEM/TEXT: name|bytes|description). Download arguments: file ID/message ID. Existing Z-prefixed commands remain ZMODEM-only. XMODEM/TEXT cannot batch. Sender/recipient authorization is identical for all protocols.\r\n")
